          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">When Is Tooth Extraction Needed?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            Our first goal is always to save natural teeth through fillings or root canal treatment. However, when a tooth is fractured below the gum, severely decayed beyond repair, extremely loose from advanced gum disease, or when a wisdom tooth pushes painfully against neighbouring teeth, removing the tooth safely stops pain and protects surrounding bone and teeth.
          </p>
